- op: discuss  # d228
  at: '2026-10-18T05:24:11Z'  # d228
  by: agent  # d228
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d228
  clock: 3  # d228
  nonce: d228  # d228
  message: "Fixed in PR #1710 (dev 629588ff98). Partial archives are per-process (<stem>.zip.<pid>.partial); _archive_entry treats FileNotFoundError on the zip, the partial->final rename and the entry->.evicting- rename as the other run's job and skips; cmd_run calls _housekeep_cache, which turns any housekeeping exception into a stderr warning. Fix-shape item (1), the flock, was NOT done: (2)+(3) make the pass tolerant without it, and a lock would only serialize work the tolerant path already handles. LIVE RE-RUN OF THE FILED REPRO (isolated XDG_CACHE_HOME, HYPERGUMBO_CACHE_MAX_GB=0.001, seeded with 8 x 20 MB entries of one repo aged 3-10 days, then 4 parallel 'hypergumbo survey' runs on tiny fixtures, 3 rounds): pre-fix df2aef43b5 = 9 of 12 runs exit 1 with 'internal error: FileNotFoundError ... results/state0 -> results/.evicting-state0'; post-fix dev = 0 of 12 non-zero, eviction ran in all 12. Production-path test: test_cache_eviction.py::test_run_exits_zero_when_eviction_raises (cli.main(['run', ...]) with eviction raising -> exit 0 + warning), plus three tests that remove the entry / partial / scratch target mid-pass. RESIDUAL found by this re-run: each racing run's summary counts entries another run moved (round 1: four runs each reported 'Soft-deleted 133.5 MB (7 stale entries)' when 7 entries existed in total). Follow-up PR next: count only what this process archived."  # d228
- op: discuss  # 9dcb
  at: '2026-10-18T07:35:42Z'  # 9dcb
  by: agent  # 9dcb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9dcb
  clock: 4  # 9dcb
  nonce: 9dcb  # 9dcb
  message: "Follow-up merged in PR #1712 (dev 8fd8c4ac00) for the residual the closure re-run found, plus one more race that re-run exposed. (1) _archive_entry returns whether THIS process moved the entry; the summary counts only those, while the cap check still counts an entry a peer took. (2) A peer sweeping our .evicting- dir as residue made our rmtree raise, ending the pass in a housekeeping warning: cache_rmtree(missing_ok=True) now finishes a tree another process is removing (retries until nothing is left; other errors still raise). (3) Residue is hard-deleted and may be a peer's in-flight scratch, so it counts toward the cap but not toward the 'Soft-deleted ... Recoverable (zipped)' summary. LIVE RE-RUN of the filed repro on the follow-up branch (same harness, 5 rounds x 4 parallel surveys): 0 of 20 runs non-zero, 0 housekeeping warnings, and the runs' reported entries sum to exactly 7 (the seeded count) in every round; before (1)+(2) round 3 summed to 6 with two 'housekeeping skipped: ... .evicting-state2' warnings, and before (1) four runs each claimed all 7. (PR #1711 carried the same commit; its pytest step was killed at 73% with zero failures after a 40-min queue behind the nightly matrix, so it was closed and re-opened as #1712.)"  # 9dcb
